    "body": "Milestone 4 · after Unit 10\nViability and route to users\nA snapshot of the same project record.\nUpdate the project record with economics, capacity, offer, acquisition or internal-adoption route, a sales/approval conversation, and onboarding. One coherent internal or external context is sufficient. Do not create another venture alongside the existing capstone.\nSeparate observation from forecast, identify missing costs, and explain the decision under a less favorable scenario. A role-play can demonstrate the conversation; actual outreach, payment, or a positive commercial result is not required.\nMilestone 4 rubricCriterion | Share | Meets the goal | Strong transfer |\nEconomics and capacity | 35% | Uses correct units and periods; separates one-time/recurring costs and cash/capacity value; includes material delivery effort and a capacity limit. | Reconciles delivery, acquisition, and support assumptions and identifies a consequential omitted-cost or double-counting risk. |\nUncertainty and decision threshold | 20% | Compares base and unfavorable scenarios and explains a correctly named break-even or decision threshold. | Explains which assumption deserves further evidence and why a favorable adjustment is or is not justified. |\nOffer and route to users | 25% | Specifies buyer/sponsor, useful promise, scope, price/resources, one channel, funnel denominators, and truthful acceptance terms. | Shows how the buyer’s alternative, delivery capacity, and acquisition economics change the offer or next step. |\nConversation and onboarding | 20% | Records a correctly labeled sales/adoption role-play or actual interaction, handles an objection with evidence, and defines onboarding and next action. | Uses a challenging response to improve the offer and distinguishes interest, agreement, use, and payment. |\n\nMissing evidence is not yet demonstrated. Partial or unreliable evidence is developing. Strong work explains a new case or alternative interpretation. A favorable business result is not required.\nBefore saving this snapshot\nCost/value and capacity table separates observations and assumptions.\nBase, unfavorable scenario, and named decision threshold agree.\nOffer promise, exclusions, price/resources, and acceptance are concrete.\nChannel and funnel identify denominator, period, and acquisition effort.\nConversation, objection, next step, and onboarding are documented accurately.\nReturn to the Finish step →"
