    "section": "Overview",
    "url": "/teaching/ai-solutions/milestone-5.html#main",
    "body": "Milestone 5 · after Unit 12\nDemonstration and handoff\nA snapshot of the same project record.\nDemonstrate the actual bounded task and defend the recommendation using the artifact, test/retest evidence, economics, and operating handoff. Provide a concise decision brief and presentation or an accessible equivalent using the offering’s announced arrangements.\nThis milestone’s internal rubric allocates 60% to the shared demonstration/handoff and 40% to individual mastery. In the full-course model, those contribute 15 and 10 percentage points respectively. The individual evidence comes from the checks near Milestones 3 and 5; do not grade it twice. Every learner explains a calculation, a decision, and a limitation. Self-paced completion does not imply instructor grading or a credential.\nMilestone 5 rubricCriterion | Share | Meets the goal | Strong transfer |\nDemonstration and evidence-backed recommendation | 25% | Shows a usable task, actual testing and revision, clear alternatives, and a recommendation proportionate to the evidence. | Connects a changed-case demonstration and the strongest contrary evidence to a well-justified next decision. |\nOperating handoff and continued use | 20% | Recipient can locate current files, sources, instructions, owner, review/exception rules, support limits, and post-course status. | A handoff trial exposes and corrects a practical issue; maintenance and closeout choices fit the actual resources. |\nExecutive communication | 15% | Concise brief and presentation use readable figures, correct units and baselines, honest claims, and a specific request. | The audience can inspect the claim-to-evidence chain and understand a material tradeoff without hidden assumptions. |\nIndividual quantitative understanding | 20% | Each learner explains a relevant calculation, units, denominator, and what changes under a new assumption. | Identifies an alternative interpretation or misleading metric and connects the correction to the decision. |\nIndividual design judgment and ownership | 20% | Each learner explains a personal contribution, consequential design choice, evidence limit, and appropriate human responsibility. | Defends a revision against a plausible alternative and transfers the reasoning to a new business condition. |\n\nMissing evidence is not yet demonstrated. Partial or unreliable evidence is developing. Strong work explains a new case or alternative interpretation. A favorable business result is not required.\nBefore saving this snapshot\nUsable artifact and actual task/test/retest records are accessible.\nRecommendation, economics, figure, uncertainty, and next request agree.\nOperating pack names owner, support boundary, maintenance, and closeout."
